import Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.Lifting
import Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Contractible

/-!
# The universal cover of a locally path-connected, semilocally simply connected space

Package WP-24b. Infrastructure the paper cites (Bredon `MR1700700`, Hatcher §1.3) and uses at
`RamcovGX.tex:292-293` (developing map on the universal covering), `:317`, `:1156`, `:1170`
(`\widetilde{Y∖S}` the universal covering of `Y∖S`) and `:1195-1196`; it carries **no ledger
label of its own**, so no label is marked here. Built in full (DEC-23), with no `sorry`.

> Recall that a connected, locally path-connected Hausdorff topological space $X$ is
> {\it semi-locally simply connected} if every $x\in X$ admit a neighborhood $\U$ such that
> every loop $\gamma$ in $X$ of base point $x$ is trivial in $X$. By standard results
> \cite{MR1700700}, it is a necessary and sufficient condition for such a topological space $X$
> to admit a universal covering. — `RamcovGX.tex:1156`

## Main declarations

* `GX.SemilocallySimplyConnected Y`: every point `y` has a neighbourhood `U` such that every loop
  at `y` **in `U`** is null-homotopic in `Y`.
* `GX.UniversalCover Y y₀`: pairs `⟨y, [γ]⟩`, `[γ]` a homotopy class rel endpoints of paths
  `y₀ ⇝ y`; topology generated by the basic sets `B(c, U) = {c · [δ] | δ a path in U}`, `U` open
  (`isTopologicalBasis`); endpoint map `UniversalCover.proj`, base point `UniversalCover.base`.
* `UniversalCover.isCoveringMap_proj`: `proj` is an `IsCoveringMap`.
* `UniversalCover.instPathConnectedSpace`, `UniversalCover.simplyConnectedSpace`,
  `UniversalCover.instLocPathConnectedSpace`: the total space is path-connected, simply
  connected and locally path-connected.
* `UniversalCover.existsUnique_lift`: for every covering `q : E → Y` and `e₀` over `y₀` there is
  a unique continuous `F` with `F base = e₀` and `q ∘ F = proj` (Mathlib's lifting criterion);
  `UniversalCover.isCoveringMap_of_comp_eq`: such an `F` is itself a covering map;
  `UniversalCover.lift_surjective`: it is onto when `E` is path-connected.
* `GX.deckGroup p`, `GX.Deck p` (`{φ : E ≃ₜ E // p ∘ φ = p}` as a subgroup);
  `UniversalCover.deckEquiv : Deck (proj Y y₀) ≃* FundamentalGroup Y y₀`.
* `GX.isCoveringMap_comp_of_finite` (alias `GX.IsCoveringMap.comp_of_finite`): `p ∘ q` is a
  covering if `p`, `q` are and `p` has finite fibres;
  `GX.isCoveringMap_comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected` (alias
  `GX.IsCoveringMap.comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected`): the same with no condition on the
  fibres when the base `Z` is locally path-connected and semilocally simply connected.
* `UniversalCover.exists_homeomorph_of_simplyConnected`: uniqueness — a simply connected, locally
  path-connected covering of `Y` is homeomorphic over `Y` to `UniversalCover Y y₀`, base point to
  any prescribed point over `y₀`.
* `GX.locPathConnectedSpace_of_isLocalHomeomorph`: local path-connectedness pulls back along a
  local homeomorphism.
* `UniversalCover.countable_fundamentalGroup`: `π₁(Y, y₀)` is countable for `Y` second
  countable, locally path-connected, semilocally simply connected.
* `GX.semilocallySimplyConnected_of_isCoveringMap`,
  `GX.semilocallySimplyConnected_iff_exists_simplyConnected_cover`: the "necessary" half of
  `:1156`, and the equivalence for path-connected, locally path-connected spaces.

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis (`:1156`, `:1195`) | here |
|---|---|
| `Y` connected | ⚠ weakened: not used for the covering, the deck group, the universal property or countability; the total space is path-connected for every `Y` (the fibre over a point not joined to `y₀` is empty). Path-connectedness is used only for surjectivity of `proj` and in the `iff` |
| `Y` locally path-connected | ✓ carried (`[LocPathConnectedSpace Y]`) wherever the topology of `Y` is used; not needed for path-connectedness of the total space |
| `Y` Hausdorff | ⚠ weakened: never used |
| `Y` semilocally simply connected | ✓ carried, in the reading of SCOPE (1) |
| `π₁` countable: `Y` second countable | ✓ carried (`[SecondCountableTopology Y]`) |
| universal property: `E` connected, locally path-connected | ⚠ weakened: nothing is assumed on `E` |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

1. `:1156` literally says "every loop $\gamma$ in $X$ of base point $x$ is trivial in $X$", which
   would make every point have trivial `π₁`; it is read as "every loop in `U`" (Hatcher's
   definition, and the paper's own `:1451-1456`). Reported as a finding.
2. The composite of two coverings is **not** a covering in general; it is proved in the two
   standard true forms — finite fibres of the second map, or a locally path-connected,
   semilocally simply connected base. The general failure (classically over a base that is not
   semilocally simply connected) is **not proved here**: no counterexample is formalized. The
   paper uses the unrestricted composition in the proof of `prop:branched_covering_composition`,
   (ii)⇒(i), at `RamcovGX.tex:1137`, over `Z₁`, an open portly subset of `Z` that is not assumed
   semilocally simply connected, with possibly infinite fibres; reported as a finding for the
   package formalizing that proposition.
3. Nothing here is about `(G,X)`-structures; the developing map is built elsewhere.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
-/

open Topology unitInterval Set Filter

namespace GX

universe u

/-! ## Semilocal simple connectedness -/

/-- A space is *semilocally simply connected* if every point `y` has a neighbourhood `U` such
that every loop at `y` contained in `U` is null-homotopic in the whole space. -/
def SemilocallySimplyConnected (Y : Type*) [TopologicalSpace Y] : Prop :=
  ∀ y : Y, ∃ U ∈ 𝓝 y, ∀ γ : Path y y, (∀ t, γ t ∈ U) → γ.Homotopic (Path.refl y)

/-- A set `W` is *good* if any two paths in `W` with the same endpoints are homotopic
(rel endpoints) in the whole space. -/
def IsGoodSet {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y] (W : Set Y) : Prop :=
  ∀ ⦃a b : Y⦄ (γ γ' : Path a b), (∀ t, γ t ∈ W) → (∀ t, γ' t ∈ W) → γ.Homotopic γ'

/-- A simply connected space is semilocally simply connected. -/
theorem SemilocallySimplyConnected.of_simplyConnectedSpace (Y : Type*) [TopologicalSpace Y]
    [SimplyConnectedSpace Y] : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y :=
  fun _ => ⟨univ, univ_mem, fun _ _ => SimplyConnectedSpace.paths_homotopic _ _⟩

/-! ## Cancellation in the fundamental groupoid -/

section Cancel
open Path.Homotopic.Quotient
variable {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y]

theorem quot_trans_left_cancel {x a b : Y} (A : Path.Homotopic.Quotient x a)
    {G G' : Path.Homotopic.Quotient a b} (h : trans A G = trans A G') : G = G' := by
  calc G = trans (trans (symm A) A) G := by rw [symm_trans, refl_trans]
    _ = trans (symm A) (trans A G) := trans_assoc _ _ _
    _ = trans (symm A) (trans A G') := by rw [h]
    _ = trans (trans (symm A) A) G' := (trans_assoc _ _ _).symm
    _ = G' := by rw [symm_trans, refl_trans]

theorem quot_trans_right_cancel {x a b : Y} {G G' : Path.Homotopic.Quotient x a}
    (A : Path.Homotopic.Quotient a b) (h : trans G A = trans G' A) : G = G' := by
  calc G = trans G (trans A (symm A)) := by rw [trans_symm, trans_refl]
    _ = trans (trans G A) (symm A) := (trans_assoc _ _ _).symm
    _ = trans (trans G' A) (symm A) := by rw [h]
    _ = trans G' (trans A (symm A)) := trans_assoc _ _ _
    _ = G' := by rw [trans_symm, trans_refl]

theorem quot_eq_of_conj_eq_refl {y a b : Y} {A : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y a}
    {G G' : Path.Homotopic.Quotient a b}
    (h : trans (trans (trans A G) (symm G')) (symm A) = refl y) : G = G' := by
  have h1 : trans (trans A G) (symm G') = A := by
    apply quot_trans_right_cancel (symm A)
    rw [h, trans_symm]
  have h2 : trans A G = trans A G' := by
    apply quot_trans_right_cancel (symm G')
    rw [h1, trans_assoc, trans_symm, trans_refl]
  exact quot_trans_left_cancel A h2

end Cancel

/-! ## Paths inside a set -/

theorem path_trans_mem {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y] {W : Set Y} {a b c : Y}
    {γ : Path a b} {γ' : Path b c} (h : ∀ t, γ t ∈ W) (h' : ∀ t, γ' t ∈ W) :
    ∀ t, (γ.trans γ') t ∈ W := by
  intro t
  have : (γ.trans γ') t ∈ range (γ.trans γ') := mem_range_self t
  rw [Path.trans_range] at this
  rcases this with ⟨s, hs⟩ | ⟨s, hs⟩
  · rw [← hs]; exact h s
  · rw [← hs]; exact h' s

theorem path_symm_mem {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y] {W : Set Y} {a b : Y}
    {γ : Path a b} (h : ∀ t, γ t ∈ W) : ∀ t, γ.symm t ∈ W := fun t => by
  rw [Path.symm_apply]; exact h _

theorem IsGoodSet.mono {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y] {W W' : Set Y} (h : IsGoodSet W)
    (hW : W' ⊆ W) : IsGoodSet W' :=
  fun _ _ γ γ' hγ hγ' => h γ γ' (fun t => hW (hγ t)) (fun t => hW (hγ' t))

/-- In a locally path-connected, semilocally simply connected space, every neighbourhood of a
point contains an open, path-connected, good neighbourhood of it. -/
theorem exists_isGoodSet {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y] [LocPathConnectedSpace Y]
    (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) (y : Y) {N : Set Y} (hN : N ∈ 𝓝 y) :
    ∃ W, IsOpen W ∧ y ∈ W ∧ W ⊆ N ∧ IsPathConnected W ∧ IsGoodSet W := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hUloop⟩ := hY y
  set V := interior (U ∩ N) with hV
  have hyV : y ∈ V := mem_interior_iff_mem_nhds.mpr (inter_mem hU hN)
  have hVU : V ⊆ U := interior_subset.trans inter_subset_left
  refine ⟨pathComponentIn V y, isOpen_interior.pathComponentIn y, mem_pathComponentIn_self hyV,
    pathComponentIn_subset.trans (interior_subset.trans inter_subset_right),
    isPathConnected_pathComponentIn hyV, ?_⟩
  intro a b γ γ' hγ hγ'
  have ha : a ∈ pathComponentIn V y := by simpa using hγ 0
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := ha
  have hγV : ∀ t, γ t ∈ V := fun t => pathComponentIn_subset (hγ t)
  have hγ'V : ∀ t, γ' t ∈ V := fun t => pathComponentIn_subset (hγ' t)
  have hL := hUloop (((α.trans γ).trans γ'.symm).trans α.symm)
    (fun t => hVU (path_trans_mem (path_trans_mem (path_trans_mem hα hγV) (path_symm_mem hγ'V))
      (path_symm_mem hα) t))
  rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.eq] at hL ⊢
  simp only [Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_trans, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_symm,
    Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_refl] at hL
  exact quot_eq_of_conj_eq_refl hL

/-! ## Evenly covered points from sheets -/

section Sheets

open Function

variable {E X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] [TopologicalSpace X]

/-- A criterion for even covering: an open `U ∋ x` whose preimage is the disjoint union of open
"sheets", each mapped bijectively onto `U` by a continuous open map. -/
theorem isEvenlyCovered_of_sheets {f : E → X} (hfc : Continuous f) (hfo : IsOpenMap f) {x : X}
    {U : Set X} (hU : IsOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U) {ι : Type*} (S : ι → Set E)
    (hS : ∀ i, IsOpen (S i)) (hinj : ∀ i, InjOn f (S i))
    (hsurj : ∀ i, SurjOn f (S i) U) (hdisj : Pairwise (Disjoint on S))
    (hcov : f ⁻¹' U ⊆ ⋃ i, S i) :
    IsEvenlyCovered f x (f ⁻¹' {x}) := by
  rcases isEmpty_or_nonempty ι with hι | hι
  · have hempty : f ⁻¹' U = ∅ := eq_empty_of_forall_notMem fun e he => by
      obtain ⟨i, -⟩ := mem_iUnion.mp (hcov he); exact hι.elim i
    have : IsEmpty (f ⁻¹' {x}) := ⟨fun ⟨e, he⟩ => by
      have : e ∈ f ⁻¹' U := by
        simp only [mem_preimage, mem_singleton_iff] at he ⊢; rw [he]; exact hxU
      rw [hempty] at this; exact this⟩
    exact .of_preimage_eq_empty _ (hU.mem_nhds hxU) hempty
  · obtain ⟨i⟩ := id hι
    obtain ⟨e, -, -⟩ := hsurj i hxU
    haveI : Nonempty (X → E) := ⟨fun _ => e⟩
    letI : TopologicalSpace ι := ⊥
    haveI : DiscreteTopology ι := ⟨rfl⟩
    have open_iff : ∀ i {W : Set X}, W ⊆ U → (IsOpen W ↔ IsOpen (f ⁻¹' W ∩ S i)) := by
      intro i W hW
      refine ⟨fun h => (h.preimage hfc).inter (hS i), fun h => ?_⟩
      have : f '' (f ⁻¹' W ∩ S i) = W := by
        refine subset_antisymm (fun _ ⟨e, he, hfe⟩ => hfe ▸ he.1) fun w hw => ?_
        obtain ⟨e, he, hfe⟩ := hsurj i (hW hw)
        exact ⟨e, ⟨by rw [mem_preimage, hfe]; exact hw, he⟩, hfe⟩
      rw [← this]; exact hfo _ h
    let t := hU.trivializationDiscrete S U open_iff hinj hsurj hdisj hcov
    have hxt : x ∈ t.baseSet := by
      simp only [t, IsOpen.trivializationDiscrete_baseSet]; exact hxU
    exact (IsEvenlyCovered.of_trivialization (t := t) hxt).to_isEvenlyCovered_preimage

/-- The sheets of an evenly covered neighbourhood. -/
theorem IsEvenlyCovered.exists_sheets {f : E → X} {x : X} {J : Type*} [TopologicalSpace J]
    (h : IsEvenlyCovered f x J) :
    ∃ U : Set X, IsOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧ ∃ S : J → Set E, (∀ i, IsOpen (S i)) ∧
      (∀ i, InjOn f (S i)) ∧ (∀ i, MapsTo f (S i) U) ∧ (∀ i, SurjOn f (S i) U) ∧
      Pairwise (Disjoint on S) ∧ f ⁻¹' U ⊆ ⋃ i, S i := by
  obtain ⟨hI, U, hxU, hU, hfU, H, hH⟩ := h
  refine ⟨U, hU, hxU, fun i => Subtype.val '' (H ⁻¹' (univ ×ˢ {i})), fun i => ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_,
    ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact hfU.isOpenMap_subtype_val _
      ((isOpen_univ.prod (isOpen_discrete _)).preimage H.continuous)
  · rintro i _ ⟨e, he, rfl⟩ _ ⟨e', he', rfl⟩ hee'
    have h1 : (H e).2 = i := by simpa using he
    have h2 : (H e').2 = i := by simpa using he'
    have : H e = H e' := Prod.ext (Subtype.ext (by rw [hH, hH]; exact hee')) (h1.trans h2.symm)
    rw [H.injective this]
  · rintro i _ ⟨e, -, rfl⟩
    exact e.2
  · intro i u hu
    refine ⟨H.symm (⟨u, hu⟩, i), ⟨_, by simp, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    have := hH (H.symm (⟨u, hu⟩, i))
    rw [Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply] at this
    exact this.symm
  · intro i j hij
    rw [Function.onFun, disjoint_left]
    rintro _ ⟨e, he, rfl⟩ ⟨e', he', hee⟩
    obtain rfl := Subtype.val_injective hee
    have h1 : (H e').2 = i := by simpa using he
    have h2 : (H e').2 = j := by simpa using he'
    exact hij (h1.symm.trans h2)
  · intro e he
    exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨(H ⟨e, he⟩).2, ⟨e, he⟩, by simp, rfl⟩

end Sheets

/-! ## Local path-connectedness lifts along local homeomorphisms -/

/-- A space admitting a local homeomorphism to a locally path-connected space is locally
path-connected (e.g. the total space of a covering of a locally path-connected space). -/
theorem locPathConnectedSpace_of_isLocalHomeomorph {X Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X]
    [TopologicalSpace Y] [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] {f : X → Y} (hf : IsLocalHomeomorph f) :
    LocPathConnectedSpace X := by
  rw [locPathConnectedSpace_iff_pathComponentIn_mem_nhds]
  intro x u hu hxu
  obtain ⟨e, hxe, rfl⟩ := hf x
  set V := e '' (e.source ∩ u) with hVdef
  have hV : IsOpen V := e.isOpen_image_source_inter hu
  have hVt : V ⊆ e.target := by
    rintro _ ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩; exact e.map_source hw.1
  have hW : IsOpen (pathComponentIn V (e x)) := hV.pathComponentIn _
  refine mem_of_superset ((e.isOpen_inter_preimage hW).mem_nhds
    ⟨hxe, mem_pathComponentIn_self ⟨x, ⟨hxe, hxu⟩, rfl⟩⟩) ?_
  rintro x' ⟨hx's, hx'W⟩
  have h := (show JoinedIn V (e x) (e x') from hx'W).map_continuousOn
    (e.continuousOn_symm.mono hVt)
  rw [e.left_inv hxe, e.left_inv hx's] at h
  refine h.mono ?_
  rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [e.left_inv hw.1]; exact hw.2

/-! ## The universal cover as a type -/

/-- The points of the universal cover of `Y` at `y₀`: an endpoint `pt` and a homotopy class
(rel endpoints) of paths from `y₀` to `pt`. -/
@[ext]
structure UniversalCover (Y : Type u) [TopologicalSpace Y] (y₀ : Y) : Type u where
  /-- The endpoint. -/
  pt : Y
  /-- The homotopy class of paths from `y₀` to `pt`. -/
  cls : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ pt

namespace UniversalCover

variable {Y : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Y] {y₀ : Y}

/-- The endpoint map of the universal cover. -/
abbrev proj (Y : Type u) [TopologicalSpace Y] (y₀ : Y) : UniversalCover Y y₀ → Y :=
  UniversalCover.pt

/-- The base point: the class of the constant path. -/
def base (y₀ : Y) : UniversalCover Y y₀ := ⟨y₀, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀⟩

/-- The basic set `B(c, U)`: the points `c · [δ]` for `δ` a path in `U` starting at `c.pt`. -/
def basic (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) (U : Set Y) : Set (UniversalCover Y y₀) :=
  {c' | ∃ δ : Path c.pt c'.pt, (∀ t, δ t ∈ U) ∧
    c'.cls = c.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)}

/-- The topology of the universal cover: generated by the basic sets over open sets. -/
instance : TopologicalSpace (UniversalCover Y y₀) :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom {S | ∃ c U, IsOpen U ∧ S = basic c U}

theorem mk_trans_eq {a a' b b' : Y} {c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ a}
    {c' : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ a'} {d : Path.Homotopic.Quotient a b}
    {d' : Path.Homotopic.Quotient a' b'} (ha : a = a') (hb : b = b') (hc : c ≍ c')
    (hd : d ≍ d') : (⟨b, c.trans d⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) = ⟨b', c'.trans d'⟩ := by
  subst ha hb; cases hc; cases hd; rfl

theorem mem_basic_self {c : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (h : c.pt ∈ U) : c ∈ basic c U :=
  ⟨Path.refl _, fun _ => h, by
    rw [Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_refl, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_refl]⟩

theorem pt_mem_of_mem_basic {c c' : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (h : c' ∈ basic c U) :
    c'.pt ∈ U ∧ c.pt ∈ U := by
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, -⟩ := h
  exact ⟨by simpa using hδ 1, by simpa using hδ 0⟩

theorem basic_mono {c : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U V : Set Y} (h : U ⊆ V) :
    basic c U ⊆ basic c V :=
  fun _ ⟨δ, hδ, e⟩ => ⟨δ, fun t => h (hδ t), e⟩

theorem basic_subset_of_mem {c c' : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (h : c' ∈ basic c U) :
    basic c' U ⊆ basic c U := by
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, e⟩ := h
  rintro c'' ⟨δ', hδ', e'⟩
  refine ⟨δ.trans δ', path_trans_mem hδ hδ', ?_⟩
  rw [e', e, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_trans, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_assoc]

theorem mem_basic_symm {c c' : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (h : c' ∈ basic c U) :
    c ∈ basic c' U := by
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, e⟩ := h
  refine ⟨δ.symm, path_symm_mem hδ, ?_⟩
  rw [e, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_symm, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_assoc,
    Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_symm, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_refl]

theorem basic_eq_of_mem {c c' : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (h : c' ∈ basic c U) :
    basic c' U = basic c U :=
  (basic_subset_of_mem h).antisymm (basic_subset_of_mem (mem_basic_symm h))

theorem isOpen_basic (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) {U : Set Y} (hU : IsOpen U) :
    IsOpen (basic c U) :=
  TopologicalSpace.isOpen_generateFrom_of_mem ⟨c, U, hU, rfl⟩

theorem basic_mem_nhds {c : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (hU : IsOpen U) (hc : c.pt ∈ U) :
    basic c U ∈ 𝓝 c :=
  (isOpen_basic c hU).mem_nhds (mem_basic_self hc)

/-- The basic sets form a basis of the topology. -/
theorem isTopologicalBasis :
    TopologicalSpace.IsTopologicalBasis
      {S : Set (UniversalCover Y y₀) | ∃ c U, IsOpen U ∧ S = basic c U} where
  exists_subset_inter := by
    rintro _ ⟨c, U, hU, rfl⟩ _ ⟨c', V, hV, rfl⟩ c'' ⟨h1, h2⟩
    refine ⟨basic c'' (U ∩ V), ⟨c'', U ∩ V, hU.inter hV, rfl⟩,
      mem_basic_self ⟨(pt_mem_of_mem_basic h1).1, (pt_mem_of_mem_basic h2).1⟩, ?_⟩
    exact subset_inter ((basic_mono inter_subset_left).trans (basic_eq_of_mem h1).le)
      ((basic_mono inter_subset_right).trans (basic_eq_of_mem h2).le)
  sUnion_eq := eq_univ_of_forall fun c =>
    ⟨basic c univ, ⟨c, univ, isOpen_univ, rfl⟩, mem_basic_self (mem_univ _)⟩
  eq_generateFrom := rfl

theorem mem_nhds_iff {c : UniversalCover Y y₀} {s : Set (UniversalCover Y y₀)} :
    s ∈ 𝓝 c ↔ ∃ U, IsOpen U ∧ c.pt ∈ U ∧ basic c U ⊆ s := by
  rw [isTopologicalBasis.mem_nhds_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨_, ⟨c', U, hU, rfl⟩, hc, hs⟩
    exact ⟨U, hU, (pt_mem_of_mem_basic hc).1, (basic_eq_of_mem hc).le.trans hs⟩
  · rintro ⟨U, hU, hc, hs⟩
    exact ⟨_, ⟨c, U, hU, rfl⟩, mem_basic_self hc, hs⟩

theorem continuous_proj : Continuous (proj Y y₀) := by
  rw [continuous_def]
  intro s hs
  rw [isOpen_iff_mem_nhds]
  intro c hc
  exact mem_of_superset (basic_mem_nhds hs hc) fun c' h => (pt_mem_of_mem_basic h).1

theorem proj_image_basic (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) (U : Set Y) :
    proj Y y₀ '' basic c U = pathComponentIn U c.pt := by
  ext y
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨c', ⟨δ, hδ, -⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨δ, hδ⟩
  · rintro ⟨δ, hδ⟩
    exact ⟨⟨y, c.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩, ⟨δ, hδ, rfl⟩, rfl⟩

theorem isOpenMap_proj [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] : IsOpenMap (proj Y y₀) := by
  rw [isTopologicalBasis.isOpenMap_iff]
  rintro _ ⟨c, U, hU, rfl⟩
  rw [proj_image_basic]
  exact hU.pathComponentIn _

/-- `proj` is injective on a basic set over a good set. -/
theorem injOn_basic {W : Set Y} (hW : IsGoodSet W) (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) :
    InjOn (proj Y y₀) (basic c W) := by
  rintro ⟨y, q⟩ ⟨δ, hδ, e⟩ ⟨y', q'⟩ ⟨δ', hδ', e'⟩ h
  change y = y' at h
  subst h
  change q = _ at e
  change q' = _ at e'
  rw [e, e', Path.Homotopic.Quotient.eq.mpr (hW δ δ' hδ hδ')]

/-! ### The endpoint map is a covering map -/

/-- **The endpoint map of the universal cover is a covering map** (`Y` locally path-connected and
semilocally simply connected; no connectedness is needed: over a point not joined to `y₀` the
fibre is empty). -/
theorem isCoveringMap_proj [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) :
    IsCoveringMap (proj Y y₀) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨W, hWo, hxW, -, hWc, hWg⟩ := exists_isGoodSet hY x univ_mem
  refine isEvenlyCovered_of_sheets continuous_proj isOpenMap_proj hWo hxW
    (ι := Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ x) (fun i => basic ⟨x, i⟩ W) (fun i => isOpen_basic _ hWo)
    (fun i => injOn_basic hWg _) (fun i w hw => ?_) (fun i j hij => ?_) (fun c hc => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := hWc.joinedIn x hxW w hw
    exact ⟨⟨w, i.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩, ⟨δ, hδ, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  · rw [Function.onFun, disjoint_left]
    intro c hci hcj
    apply hij
    have hj : (⟨x, j⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) ∈ basic ⟨x, i⟩ W := by
      rw [← basic_eq_of_mem hci, basic_eq_of_mem hcj]; exact mem_basic_self hxW
    have := injOn_basic hWg _ (mem_basic_self hxW) hj rfl
    exact (eq_of_heq (UniversalCover.mk.inj this).2)
  · obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := hWc.joinedIn c.pt hc x hxW
    exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨c.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ),
      mem_basic_symm (show (⟨x, c.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩ :
        UniversalCover Y y₀) ∈ basic c W from ⟨δ, hδ, rfl⟩)⟩

/-! ### The canonical lift of a path -/

/-- The affine path in `I` from `s` to `t`. -/
def segPath (s t : I) : Path s t where
  toFun r := ⟨s + r * (t - s), by
    have h1 := mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 r.2.2) s.2.1
    have h2 := mul_nonneg r.2.1 t.2.1
    have h3 := mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.2 r.2.2) (sub_nonneg.2 s.2.2)
    have h4 := mul_nonneg r.2.1 (sub_nonneg.2 t.2.2)
    constructor <;> nlinarith⟩
  continuous_toFun := by fun_prop
  source' := by ext; simp
  target' := by ext; simp

theorem segPath_apply (s t r : I) : ((segPath s t r : I) : ℝ) = s + r * (t - s) := rfl

theorem dist_segPath_le (s t r : I) : dist (segPath s t r) s ≤ dist t s := by
  rw [Subtype.dist_eq, Subtype.dist_eq, Real.dist_eq, Real.dist_eq, segPath_apply,
    show (s : ℝ) + r * (t - s) - s = r * (t - s) by ring, abs_mul, abs_of_nonneg r.2.1]
  exact mul_le_of_le_one_left (abs_nonneg _) r.2.2

/-- The unit interval is simply connected (it is convex). -/
instance instSimplyConnectedSpaceUnitInterval : SimplyConnectedSpace I := by
  haveI : ContractibleSpace I := (convex_Icc (0 : ℝ) 1).contractibleSpace ⟨0, by simp⟩
  infer_instance

/-- The canonical lift of `δ : C(I, Y)` starting at a class `c` of paths from `y₀` to `δ 0`:
`t ↦ c · [δ|[0,t]]`. -/
noncomputable def rawLift (δ : C(I, Y)) (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ (δ 0)) (t : I) : UniversalCover Y y₀ :=
  ⟨δ t, c.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk ((segPath 0 t).map δ.continuous))⟩

theorem rawLift_cls_trans (δ : C(I, Y)) (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ (δ 0)) (s t : I) :
    (rawLift δ c t).cls = (rawLift δ c s).cls.trans
      (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk ((segPath s t).map δ.continuous)) := by
  have key : Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk ((segPath 0 t).map δ.continuous) =
      (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk ((segPath 0 s).map δ.continuous)).trans
        (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk ((segPath s t).map δ.continuous)) := by
    rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_trans, ← Path.map_trans]
    exact Path.Homotopic.Quotient.eq.mpr ((SimplyConnectedSpace.paths_homotopic _ _).map δ)
  change c.trans _ = (c.trans _).trans _
  rw [key]
  exact (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_assoc _ _ _).symm

theorem rawLift_mem_basic (δ : C(I, Y)) (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ (δ 0)) {U : Set Y}
    (hU : ∀ r, δ r ∈ U) (s t : I) : rawLift δ c t ∈ basic (rawLift δ c s) U :=
  ⟨(segPath s t).map δ.continuous, fun _ => hU _, rawLift_cls_trans δ c s t⟩

theorem continuous_rawLift (δ : C(I, Y)) (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ (δ 0)) :
    Continuous (rawLift δ c) := by
  rw [continuous_iff_continuousAt]
  intro t₀
  rw [ContinuousAt, tendsto_def]
  intro s hs
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hUt, hsub⟩ := mem_nhds_iff.1 hs
  have : δ ⁻¹' U ∈ 𝓝 t₀ := δ.continuous.continuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds (hU.mem_nhds hUt)
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩ := Metric.mem_nhds_iff.1 this
  filter_upwards [Metric.ball_mem_nhds t₀ hε] with t ht
  exact hsub ⟨(segPath t₀ t).map δ.continuous,
    fun r => hball (lt_of_le_of_lt (dist_segPath_le t₀ t r) ht), rawLift_cls_trans δ c t₀ t⟩

theorem segPath_zero_zero (r : I) : segPath 0 0 r = 0 := Subtype.ext (by simp [segPath_apply])

theorem segPath_zero_one (r : I) : segPath 0 1 r = r := Subtype.ext (by simp [segPath_apply])

/-- The canonical lift of a path `δ : a ⇝ b` from the point `⟨a, c⟩`, as a path of the universal
cover ending at `⟨b, c · [δ]⟩`. -/
noncomputable def liftFrom {a b : Y} (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ a) (δ : Path a b) :
    Path (⟨a, c⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) ⟨b, c.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩ where
  toFun := rawLift δ.toContinuousMap (c.cast rfl δ.source)
  continuous_toFun := continuous_rawLift _ _
  source' := by
    change (⟨δ 0, _⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) = _
    conv_rhs => rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_refl c]
    refine mk_trans_eq δ.source δ.source (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.cast_heq _ _) ?_
    rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_refl]
    exact Path.Homotopic.hpath_hext fun r => by
      simp [Path.map_coe, segPath_zero_zero]
  target' := by
    change (⟨δ 1, _⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) = _
    refine mk_trans_eq δ.source δ.target (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.cast_heq _ _) ?_
    exact Path.Homotopic.hpath_hext fun r => by
      simp [Path.map_coe, segPath_zero_one]

theorem liftFrom_apply {a b : Y} (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ a) (δ : Path a b) (t : I) :
    liftFrom c δ t = rawLift δ.toContinuousMap (c.cast rfl δ.source) t := rfl

theorem proj_liftFrom {a b : Y} (c : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ a) (δ : Path a b) (t : I) :
    (liftFrom c δ t).pt = δ t := rfl

/-! ### Path-connectedness, simple connectedness, local path-connectedness -/

/-- **The universal cover is path-connected** (no hypothesis on `Y`). -/
instance : PathConnectedSpace (UniversalCover Y y₀) := by
  have hj : ∀ c : UniversalCover Y y₀, Joined (base y₀) c := by
    rintro ⟨y, q⟩
    induction q using Path.Homotopic.Quotient.ind with
    | mk γ =>
      have := liftFrom (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀) γ
      rw [Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl_trans] at this
      exact ⟨this⟩
  exact ⟨⟨base y₀⟩, fun c c' => (hj c).symm.trans (hj c')⟩

/-- **The universal cover is simply connected.** -/
theorem simplyConnectedSpace [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) :
    SimplyConnectedSpace (UniversalCover Y y₀) := by
  rw [simply_connected_iff_loops_nullhomotopic]
  refine ⟨inferInstance, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨y, q⟩ Γ
  have hp := isCoveringMap_proj (y₀ := y₀) hY
  let δ : Path y y := Γ.map continuous_proj
  have hL : (Γ : I → UniversalCover Y y₀) = liftFrom q δ :=
    hp.eq_of_comp_eq Γ.continuous (liftFrom q δ).continuous (funext fun t => rfl) 0
      (by rw [Path.source, Path.source])
  have h1 : Γ 1 = liftFrom q δ 1 := congrFun hL 1
  rw [Path.target, Path.target] at h1
  have h2 : q = q.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ) := eq_of_heq (UniversalCover.mk.inj h1).2
  have h3 : Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ = Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y := by
    apply quot_trans_left_cancel q
    rw [← h2, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_refl]
  rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.eq]
  apply hp.injective_path_homotopic_map
  change (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk Γ).map _ = (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk (Path.refl _)).map _
  rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_map, ← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_map]
  refine h3.trans ?_
  rw [← Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk_refl]
  congr 1

/-- A basic set is path-connected. -/
theorem isPathConnected_basic {c : UniversalCover Y y₀} {U : Set Y} (hcU : c.pt ∈ U) :
    IsPathConnected (basic c U) := by
  refine ⟨c, mem_basic_self hcU, fun {c'} hc' => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ, e⟩ := hc'
  have hc : (⟨c.pt, c.cls⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) = c := rfl
  have hc'' : (⟨c'.pt, c.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) =
      c' := by rw [← e]
  refine ⟨((liftFrom c.cls δ).cast hc.symm hc''.symm), fun t => ?_⟩
  have h0 : rawLift δ.toContinuousMap (c.cls.cast rfl δ.source) 0 = c :=
    (liftFrom c.cls δ).source
  have := rawLift_mem_basic δ.toContinuousMap (c.cls.cast rfl δ.source) hδ 0 t
  rw [h0] at this
  exact this

/-- **The universal cover is locally path-connected.** -/
instance [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] : LocPathConnectedSpace (UniversalCover Y y₀) := by
  refine LocPathConnectedSpace.of_bases
    (p := fun c (U : Set Y) => IsOpen U ∧ c.pt ∈ U ∧ IsPathConnected U)
    (s := fun c U => basic c U) (fun c => ⟨fun t => ⟨fun ht => ?_, ?_⟩⟩) ?_
  · obtain ⟨U, hU, hcU, hsub⟩ := mem_nhds_iff.1 ht
    exact ⟨pathComponentIn U c.pt, ⟨hU.pathComponentIn _, mem_pathComponentIn_self hcU,
      isPathConnected_pathComponentIn hcU⟩, (basic_mono pathComponentIn_subset).trans hsub⟩
  · rintro ⟨U, ⟨hU, hcU, -⟩, hs⟩
    exact mem_of_superset (basic_mem_nhds hU hcU) hs
  · rintro c U ⟨-, hcU, -⟩
    exact isPathConnected_basic hcU

/-! ### The universal property -/

/-- **Universal property.** For every covering map `q : E → Y` and every `e₀` over `y₀`, there is
a unique continuous map `F` from the universal cover to `E` over `Y` (a morphism of coverings)
sending the base point to `e₀`. No hypothesis on `E` is needed. -/
theorem existsUnique_lift [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y)
    {E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] {q : E → Y} (hq : IsCoveringMap q) {e₀ : E}
    (he : q e₀ = y₀) :
    ∃! F : C(UniversalCover Y y₀, E), F (base y₀) = e₀ ∧ q ∘ F = proj Y y₀ := by
  haveI := simplyConnectedSpace (y₀ := y₀) hY
  exact hq.existsUnique_continuousMap_lifts ⟨proj Y y₀, continuous_proj⟩ (base y₀) e₀ he

/-- The morphism of the universal property is surjective when `E` is path-connected. -/
theorem lift_surjective [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] {E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E]
    [PathConnectedSpace E] {q : E → Y} (hq : IsCoveringMap q) {e₀ : E} (he : q e₀ = y₀)
    (F : C(UniversalCover Y y₀, E)) (hF0 : F (base y₀) = e₀) (hF : q ∘ F = proj Y y₀) :
    Function.Surjective F := by
  intro e
  obtain ⟨γ⟩ := PathConnectedSpace.joined e₀ e
  let δ : Path y₀ (q e) := (γ.map hq.continuous).cast he.symm rfl
  let Λ : Path (base y₀) _ := liftFrom (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀) δ
  refine ⟨Λ 1, ?_⟩
  have h : (F ∘ Λ : I → E) = γ := by
    refine hq.eq_of_comp_eq (F.continuous.comp Λ.continuous) γ.continuous ?_ 0 ?_
    · funext t
      change (q ∘ F) (Λ t) = q (γ t)
      rw [hF]; rfl
    · change F (Λ 0) = γ 0
      rw [Λ.source, hF0, γ.source]
  have := congrFun h 1
  simpa using this

/-- A preconnected set covered by pairwise disjoint open sets lies in one of them. -/
theorem _root_.GX.IsPreconnected.subset_of_pairwise_disjoint {E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E]
    {ι : Type*} {T : ι → Set E} (hT : ∀ j, IsOpen (T j)) (hd : Pairwise (Function.onFun Disjoint T))
    {s : Set E} (hs : IsPreconnected s) (hcov : s ⊆ ⋃ j, T j) {j : ι} (hj : (s ∩ T j).Nonempty) :
    s ⊆ T j := by
  refine hs.subset_left_of_subset_union (v := ⋃ k ∈ {k | k ≠ j}, T k) (hT j)
    (isOpen_biUnion fun k _ => hT k) ?_ ?_ hj
  · rw [disjoint_iUnion₂_right]
    exact fun k hk => hd (Ne.symm hk)
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hcov hx)
    by_cases hkj : k = j
    · subst hkj; exact Or.inl hk
    · exact Or.inr (mem_biUnion hkj hk)

/-- **The morphism of the universal property is itself a covering map** (no hypothesis on `E`). -/
theorem isCoveringMap_of_comp_eq [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y)
    {E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] {q : E → Y} (hq : IsCoveringMap q)
    {F : UniversalCover Y y₀ → E} (hFc : Continuous F) (hF : q ∘ F = proj Y y₀) :
    IsCoveringMap F := by
  have hp := isCoveringMap_proj (y₀ := y₀) hY
  have hFl : IsLocalHomeomorph F :=
    IsLocalHomeomorph.of_comp (hF ▸ hp.isLocalHomeomorph) hq.isLocalHomeomorph hFc
  have hqF : ∀ a, q (F a) = a.pt := fun a => congrFun hF a
  intro e
  obtain ⟨Uq, hUqo, hxUq, T, hTo, hTi, -, -, hTd, hTc⟩ := IsEvenlyCovered.exists_sheets (hq (q e))
  obtain ⟨W, hWo, hxW, hWUq, hWc, hWg⟩ := exists_isGoodSet hY (q e) (hUqo.mem_nhds hxUq)
  obtain ⟨j₀, hej₀⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hTc hxUq)
  -- the image of a basic set over `W` lies in a single sheet
  have hsheet : ∀ a : UniversalCover Y y₀, a.pt ∈ W → F a ∈ T j₀ → F '' basic a W ⊆ T j₀ := by
    intro a haW haT
    refine GX.IsPreconnected.subset_of_pairwise_disjoint hTo hTd
      ((isPathConnected_basic haW).image hFc).isConnected.isPreconnected ?_
      ⟨F a, ⟨a, mem_basic_self haW, rfl⟩, haT⟩
    rintro _ ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩
    apply hTc
    rw [mem_preimage, hqF]
    exact hWUq (pt_mem_of_mem_basic hb).1
  have hinj : ∀ a : UniversalCover Y y₀, InjOn F (basic a W) := fun a b hb b' hb' h =>
    injOn_basic hWg a hb hb' (by change b.pt = b'.pt; rw [← hqF, ← hqF, h])
  refine isEvenlyCovered_of_sheets hFc hFl.isOpenMap ((hTo j₀).inter (hWo.preimage hq.continuous))
    ⟨hej₀, hxW⟩ (ι := {a : UniversalCover Y y₀ // a.pt = q e ∧ F a ∈ T j₀})
    (fun a => basic a.1 W) (fun a => isOpen_basic _ hWo) (fun a => hinj a.1) ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rintro ⟨a, ha, haT⟩ t ⟨htT, htW⟩
    obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := hWc.joinedIn a.pt (ha ▸ hxW) (q t) htW
    let a' : UniversalCover Y y₀ := ⟨q t, a.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩
    have ha' : a' ∈ basic a W := ⟨δ, hδ, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨a', ha', hTi j₀ (hsheet a (ha ▸ hxW) haT ⟨a', ha', rfl⟩) htT ?_⟩
    rw [hqF]
  · rintro ⟨a, ha, _haT⟩ ⟨b, hb, _hbT⟩ hab
    rw [Function.onFun, disjoint_left]
    intro c hca hcb
    apply hab
    have hb' : b ∈ basic a W := by
      rw [← basic_eq_of_mem hca, basic_eq_of_mem hcb]
      exact mem_basic_self (by rw [hb]; exact hxW)
    exact Subtype.ext (injOn_basic hWg a (mem_basic_self (by rw [ha]; exact hxW)) hb'
      (ha.trans hb.symm))
  · intro c hc
    obtain ⟨hcT, hcW⟩ := hc
    have hcW' : c.pt ∈ W := by rw [← hqF]; exact hcW
    obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := hWc.joinedIn c.pt hcW' (q e) hxW
    let a : UniversalCover Y y₀ := ⟨q e, c.cls.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk δ)⟩
    have ha : a ∈ basic c W := ⟨δ, hδ, rfl⟩
    exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨a, rfl, hsheet c hcW' hcT ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩⟩, mem_basic_symm ha⟩

/-! ### Uniqueness up to isomorphism -/

/-- **Uniqueness of the universal cover.** A covering `q : E → Y` with `E` simply connected and
locally path-connected is isomorphic over `Y` to `UniversalCover Y y₀`, by a homeomorphism sending
the base point to any prescribed `e₀` over `y₀`. Together with `existsUnique_lift` this is the
"maximal among coverings, unique up to isomorphism" used at `RamcovGX.tex:1156` and `:1185-1186`. -/
theorem exists_homeomorph_of_simplyConnected [LocPathConnectedSpace Y]
    (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) {E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] [SimplyConnectedSpace E]
    [LocPathConnectedSpace E] {q : E → Y} (hq : IsCoveringMap q) {e₀ : E} (he : q e₀ = y₀) :
    ∃ Φ : UniversalCover Y y₀ ≃ₜ E, Φ (base y₀) = e₀ ∧ q ∘ Φ = proj Y y₀ := by
  haveI := simplyConnectedSpace (y₀ := y₀) hY
  have hp := isCoveringMap_proj (y₀ := y₀) hY
  obtain ⟨F, ⟨hF0, hF⟩, -⟩ := existsUnique_lift hY hq he
  obtain ⟨G, ⟨hG0, hG⟩, -⟩ :=
    hp.existsUnique_continuousMap_lifts ⟨q, hq.continuous⟩ e₀ (base y₀) he.symm
  have hGF : G.comp F = ContinuousMap.id _ := by
    obtain ⟨_, _, huniq⟩ :=
      hp.existsUnique_continuousMap_lifts ⟨proj Y y₀, continuous_proj⟩ (base y₀) (base y₀) rfl
    refine (huniq _ ⟨?_, ?_⟩).trans (huniq _ ⟨rfl, rfl⟩).symm
    · simp [hF0, hG0]
    · ext c
      change proj Y y₀ (G (F c)) = proj Y y₀ c
      rw [show proj Y y₀ (G (F c)) = q (F c) from congrFun hG (F c)]
      exact congrFun hF c
  have hFG : F.comp G = ContinuousMap.id _ := by
    obtain ⟨_, _, huniq⟩ :=
      hq.existsUnique_continuousMap_lifts ⟨q, hq.continuous⟩ e₀ e₀ rfl
    refine (huniq _ ⟨?_, ?_⟩).trans (huniq _ ⟨rfl, rfl⟩).symm
    · simp [hF0, hG0]
    · ext e
      change q (F (G e)) = q e
      rw [show q (F (G e)) = proj Y y₀ (G e) from congrFun hF (G e)]
      exact congrFun hG e
  let Φ : UniversalCover Y y₀ ≃ₜ E :=
    { toFun := F
      invFun := G
      left_inv := fun c => DFunLike.congr_fun hGF c
      right_inv := fun e => DFunLike.congr_fun hFG e
      continuous_toFun := F.continuous
      continuous_invFun := G.continuous }
  exact ⟨Φ, hF0, hF⟩

/-! ### Semilocal simple connectedness is necessary -/

/-- The endpoint map is surjective when `Y` is path-connected. -/
theorem proj_surjective [PathConnectedSpace Y] : Function.Surjective (proj Y y₀) := fun y =>
  ⟨⟨y, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk (PathConnectedSpace.somePath y₀ y)⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **Conversely, a space admitting a simply connected (surjective) covering is semilocally
simply connected.** -/
theorem _root_.GX.semilocallySimplyConnected_of_isCoveringMap {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y]
    {E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] [SimplyConnectedSpace E] {q : E → Y}
    (hq : IsCoveringMap q) (hsurj : Function.Surjective q) : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨e, rfl⟩ := hsurj y
  obtain ⟨U, hUo, hxU, T, hTo, hTi, -, -, hTd, hTc⟩ := IsEvenlyCovered.exists_sheets (hq (q e))
  obtain ⟨j, hej⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hTc hxU)
  refine ⟨U, hUo.mem_nhds hxU, fun γ hγ => ?_⟩
  let Γ := hq.liftPath γ e γ.source
  have hΓq : ∀ t, q (Γ t) = γ t := fun t => congrFun (hq.liftPath_lifts γ e γ.source) t
  have hΓ0 : Γ 0 = e := hq.liftPath_zero γ e γ.source
  have hsub : range Γ ⊆ T j := by
    refine GX.IsPreconnected.subset_of_pairwise_disjoint hTo hTd
      (isConnected_range Γ.continuous).isPreconnected ?_ ⟨e, ⟨0, hΓ0⟩, hej⟩
    rintro _ ⟨t, rfl⟩
    apply hTc
    rw [mem_preimage, hΓq]
    exact hγ t
  have hΓ1 : Γ 1 = e := hTi j (hsub ⟨1, rfl⟩) hej (by rw [hΓq, γ.target])
  let Λ : Path e e := ⟨Γ, hΓ0, hΓ1⟩
  have h := (SimplyConnectedSpace.paths_homotopic Λ (Path.refl e)).map ⟨q, hq.continuous⟩
  have h1 : γ = Λ.map hq.continuous := Path.ext (funext fun t => (hΓq t).symm)
  have h2 : Path.refl (q e) = (Path.refl e).map hq.continuous := Path.ext (funext fun t => rfl)
  rw [h1, h2]
  exact h

/-- **For a path-connected, locally path-connected space, semilocal simple connectedness is
equivalent to the existence of a simply connected covering.** The right-hand side quantifies over
`E : Type u`, `Y`'s universe; the converse for a covering in any universe is
`semilocallySimplyConnected_of_isCoveringMap`. -/
theorem _root_.GX.semilocallySimplyConnected_iff_exists_simplyConnected_cover
    [PathConnectedSpace Y] [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] :
    SemilocallySimplyConnected Y ↔ ∃ (E : Type u) (_ : TopologicalSpace E),
      SimplyConnectedSpace E ∧ ∃ q : E → Y, IsCoveringMap q ∧ Function.Surjective q := by
  constructor
  · intro hY
    obtain ⟨y₀⟩ := (inferInstance : Nonempty Y)
    exact ⟨UniversalCover Y y₀, inferInstance, simplyConnectedSpace hY, proj Y y₀,
      isCoveringMap_proj hY, proj_surjective⟩
  · rintro ⟨E, _, _, q, hq, hs⟩
    exact semilocallySimplyConnected_of_isCoveringMap hq hs

/-! ### The deck group -/

end UniversalCover

section Deck

variable {E X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E]

/-- The deck transformations of `p : E → X`, as a subgroup of the homeomorphism group. -/
def deckGroup (p : E → X) : Subgroup (E ≃ₜ E) where
  carrier := {φ | p ∘ φ = p}
  mul_mem' {φ ψ} hφ hψ := by
    simp only [mem_setOf_eq] at hφ hψ ⊢
    funext x
    change p (φ (ψ x)) = p x
    have h1 := congrFun hφ (ψ x)
    have h2 := congrFun hψ x
    simp only [Function.comp_apply] at h1 h2
    rw [h1, h2]
  one_mem' := rfl
  inv_mem' {φ} hφ := by
    simp only [mem_setOf_eq] at hφ ⊢
    funext x
    have := congrFun hφ (φ.symm x)
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, Homeomorph.apply_symm_apply] at this
    rw [Function.comp_apply, Homeomorph.inv_apply, ← this]

/-- The deck group `Deck p = {φ : E ≃ₜ E // p ∘ φ = p}`. -/
abbrev Deck (p : E → X) : Type _ := deckGroup p

theorem mem_deckGroup_iff (p : E → X) (φ : E ≃ₜ E) : φ ∈ deckGroup p ↔ p ∘ φ = p := Iff.rfl

end Deck

namespace UniversalCover

variable {Y : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Y] {y₀ : Y}

/-- Left multiplication by a loop class at `y₀`: `⟨y, c⟩ ↦ ⟨y, g · c⟩`. -/
noncomputable def leftMul (g : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ y₀) (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) :
    UniversalCover Y y₀ :=
  ⟨c.pt, g.trans c.cls⟩

theorem continuous_leftMul (g : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ y₀) : Continuous (leftMul g) := by
  rw [continuous_iff_continuousAt]
  intro c
  rw [ContinuousAt, tendsto_def]
  intro s hs
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hcU, hsub⟩ := mem_nhds_iff.1 hs
  filter_upwards [basic_mem_nhds hU hcU] with c' ⟨δ, hδ, e⟩
  refine hsub ⟨δ, hδ, ?_⟩
  change g.trans c'.cls = (g.trans c.cls).trans _
  rw [e, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_assoc]
  rfl

theorem leftMul_leftMul (g h : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ y₀) (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) :
    leftMul g (leftMul h c) = leftMul (g.trans h) c := by
  simp only [leftMul, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_assoc]

theorem leftMul_refl (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) :
    leftMul (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀) c = c := by
  simp only [leftMul, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl_trans]

/-- Left multiplication as a homeomorphism. -/
noncomputable def leftMulHomeomorph (g : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ y₀) :
    UniversalCover Y y₀ ≃ₜ UniversalCover Y y₀ where
  toFun := leftMul g
  invFun := leftMul g.symm
  left_inv c := by
    rw [leftMul_leftMul, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.symm_trans, leftMul_refl]
  right_inv c := by
    rw [leftMul_leftMul, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_symm, leftMul_refl]
  continuous_toFun := continuous_leftMul g
  continuous_invFun := continuous_leftMul g.symm

theorem toPath_one : FundamentalGroup.toPath (1 : FundamentalGroup Y y₀) =
    Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀ := rfl

theorem toPath_mul (a b : FundamentalGroup Y y₀) :
    FundamentalGroup.toPath (a * b) =
      (FundamentalGroup.toPath b).trans (FundamentalGroup.toPath a) := rfl

/-- The action of `π₁(Y, y₀)` on the universal cover by deck transformations. -/
noncomputable def deckHom : FundamentalGroup Y y₀ →* Deck (proj Y y₀) where
  toFun g := ⟨leftMulHomeomorph (FundamentalGroup.toPath g⁻¹), rfl⟩
  map_one' := by
    refine Subtype.ext (Homeomorph.ext fun c => ?_)
    change leftMul (FundamentalGroup.toPath (1 : FundamentalGroup Y y₀)⁻¹) c = c
    rw [inv_one, toPath_one, leftMul_refl]
  map_mul' a b := by
    refine Subtype.ext (Homeomorph.ext fun c => ?_)
    change leftMul (FundamentalGroup.toPath (a * b)⁻¹) c =
      leftMul (FundamentalGroup.toPath a⁻¹) (leftMul (FundamentalGroup.toPath b⁻¹) c)
    rw [mul_inv_rev, toPath_mul, leftMul_leftMul]

theorem deckHom_apply (g : FundamentalGroup Y y₀) (c : UniversalCover Y y₀) :
    (deckHom g).1 c =
      leftMul (FundamentalGroup.toPath g⁻¹) c := rfl

theorem deckHom_injective : Function.Injective (deckHom (Y := Y) (y₀ := y₀)) := by
  rw [injective_iff_map_eq_one]
  intro g hg
  have h := congrArg (fun φ : Deck (proj Y y₀) => φ.1 (base y₀)) hg
  simp only [deckHom_apply] at h
  change (⟨y₀, (FundamentalGroup.toPath g⁻¹).trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀)⟩ :
    UniversalCover Y y₀) = ⟨y₀, Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀⟩ at h
  have h' := eq_of_heq (UniversalCover.mk.inj h).2
  rw [Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_refl] at h'
  have : g⁻¹ = 1 := h'
  exact inv_eq_one.mp this

theorem deckHom_surjective [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) :
    Function.Surjective (deckHom (Y := Y) (y₀ := y₀)) := by
  intro ψ
  have hp := isCoveringMap_proj (y₀ := y₀) hY
  set c := ψ.1 (base y₀) with hcdef
  have hc : c.pt = y₀ := congrFun ψ.2 (base y₀)
  let g' : Path.Homotopic.Quotient y₀ y₀ := c.cls.cast rfl hc.symm
  refine ⟨(FundamentalGroup.fromPath g')⁻¹, Subtype.ext (Homeomorph.ext fun x => ?_)⟩
  rw [deckHom_apply, inv_inv]
  refine congrFun (hp.eq_of_comp_eq (continuous_leftMul g') ψ.1.continuous ?_ (base y₀) ?_) x
  · funext x
    exact (congrFun ψ.2 x).symm
  · rw [← hcdef]
    change (⟨y₀, g'.trans (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.refl y₀)⟩ : UniversalCover Y y₀) = c
    rw [Path.Homotopic.Quotient.trans_refl]
    exact UniversalCover.ext hc.symm (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.cast_heq _ _)

/-- **`Deck(Ỹ) ≃* π₁(Y, y₀)`** for the universal cover of a locally path-connected,
semilocally simply connected space. -/
noncomputable def deckEquiv [LocPathConnectedSpace Y] (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) :
    Deck (proj Y y₀) ≃* FundamentalGroup Y y₀ :=
  (MulEquiv.ofBijective deckHom ⟨deckHom_injective, deckHom_surjective hY⟩).symm

/-! ### Countability of the fundamental group -/

end UniversalCover

/-- A chain argument: in a preconnected space covered by open sets each of which meets only
countably many members of the cover, countably many members already cover. -/
theorem exists_countable_cover_of_chain {Z : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Z] [PreconnectedSpace Z]
    (𝒮 : Set (Set Z)) (hopen : ∀ S ∈ 𝒮, IsOpen S) (hcov : ⋃₀ 𝒮 = univ)
    (hnb : ∀ S ∈ 𝒮, {T | T ∈ 𝒮 ∧ (S ∩ T).Nonempty}.Countable) :
    ∃ 𝒮' ⊆ 𝒮, 𝒮'.Countable ∧ ⋃₀ 𝒮' = univ := by
  rcases isEmpty_or_nonempty Z with hZ | ⟨⟨z⟩⟩
  · refine ⟨∅, empty_subset _, countable_empty, ?_⟩
    rw [sUnion_empty, eq_comm, univ_eq_empty_iff]; exact hZ
  obtain ⟨S₀, hS₀, hzS₀⟩ : ∃ S ∈ 𝒮, z ∈ S := by
    have : z ∈ ⋃₀ 𝒮 := hcov ▸ mem_univ z
    exact this
  let nb : Set Z → Set (Set Z) := fun S => {T | T ∈ 𝒮 ∧ (S ∩ T).Nonempty}
  let R : ℕ → Set (Set Z) := fun n =>
    Nat.rec (motive := fun _ => Set (Set Z)) {S₀} (fun _ Rn => ⋃ S ∈ Rn, nb S) n
  have hR0 : R 0 = {S₀} := rfl
  have hRs : ∀ n, R (n + 1) = ⋃ S ∈ R n, nb S := fun n => rfl
  have hRsub : ∀ n, R n ⊆ 𝒮 ∧ (R n).Countable := by
    intro n
    induction n with
    | zero => rw [hR0]; exact ⟨singleton_subset_iff.2 hS₀, countable_singleton _⟩
    | succ n ih =>
      rw [hRs]
      exact ⟨iUnion₂_subset fun S _ T hT => hT.1, ih.2.biUnion fun S hS => hnb S (ih.1 hS)⟩
  refine ⟨⋃ n, R n, iUnion_subset fun n => (hRsub n).1, countable_iUnion fun n => (hRsub n).2, ?_⟩
  set A := ⋃₀ (⋃ n, R n) with hA
  have hAo : IsOpen A := isOpen_sUnion fun S hS => by
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 hS
    exact hopen S ((hRsub n).1 hn)
  have hAc : IsOpen Aᶜ := by
    have : Aᶜ = ⋃₀ (𝒮 \ ⋃ n, R n) := by
      ext x
      constructor
      · intro hx
        have : x ∈ ⋃₀ 𝒮 := hcov ▸ mem_univ x
        obtain ⟨T, hT, hxT⟩ := this
        exact ⟨T, ⟨hT, fun hTR => hx ⟨T, hTR, hxT⟩⟩, hxT⟩
      · rintro ⟨T, ⟨hT, hTR⟩, hxT⟩ ⟨S, hS, hxS⟩
        obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 hS
        exact hTR (mem_iUnion.2 ⟨n + 1, by rw [hRs]; exact mem_biUnion hn ⟨hT, x, hxS, hxT⟩⟩)
    rw [this]
    exact isOpen_sUnion fun T hT => hopen T hT.1
  have hAne : A.Nonempty := ⟨z, S₀, mem_iUnion.2 ⟨0, by rw [hR0]; rfl⟩, hzS₀⟩
  exact IsClopen.eq_univ ⟨isOpen_compl_iff.mp hAc, hAo⟩ hAne

namespace UniversalCover

variable {Y : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Y]

/-- **The fundamental group of a second countable, locally path-connected, semilocally simply
connected space is countable.** -/
theorem countable_fundamentalGroup [SecondCountableTopology Y] [LocPathConnectedSpace Y]
    (hY : SemilocallySimplyConnected Y) (y₀ : Y) : Countable (FundamentalGroup Y y₀) := by
  let 𝒢 : Set (Set Y) := {W | IsOpen W ∧ IsPathConnected W ∧ IsGoodSet W}
  obtain ⟨𝒢₀, h𝒢₀c, h𝒢₀s, h𝒢₀u⟩ :=
    TopologicalSpace.isOpen_sUnion_countable 𝒢 (fun W hW => hW.1)
  have hcovY : ⋃₀ 𝒢₀ = univ := by
    rw [h𝒢₀u]
    refine eq_univ_of_forall fun y => ?_
    obtain ⟨W, hWo, hyW, -, hWc, hWg⟩ := exists_isGoodSet hY y univ_mem
    exact ⟨W, ⟨hWo, hWc, hWg⟩, hyW⟩
  let 𝒮 : Set (Set (UniversalCover Y y₀)) :=
    {S | ∃ W ∈ 𝒢₀, ∃ c : UniversalCover Y y₀, c.pt ∈ W ∧ S = basic c W}
  have hopen : ∀ S ∈ 𝒮, IsOpen S := by
    rintro _ ⟨W, hW, c, -, rfl⟩
    exact isOpen_basic c (h𝒢₀s hW).1
  have hcov : ⋃₀ 𝒮 = univ := eq_univ_of_forall fun c => by
    have : c.pt ∈ ⋃₀ 𝒢₀ := hcovY ▸ mem_univ _
    obtain ⟨W, hW, hcW⟩ := this
    exact ⟨basic c W, ⟨W, hW, c, hcW, rfl⟩, mem_basic_self hcW⟩
  have hnb : ∀ S ∈ 𝒮, {T | T ∈ 𝒮 ∧ (S ∩ T).Nonempty}.Countable := by
    rintro _ ⟨W, hW, c, -, rfl⟩
    have hsub : {T | T ∈ 𝒮 ∧ (basic c W ∩ T).Nonempty} ⊆
        ⋃ W' ∈ 𝒢₀, {T | (∃ c', T = basic c' W') ∧ (basic c W ∩ T).Nonempty} := by
      rintro _ ⟨⟨W', hW', c', -, rfl⟩, hne⟩
      exact mem_biUnion hW' ⟨⟨c', rfl⟩, hne⟩
    refine Countable.mono hsub (h𝒢₀c.biUnion fun W' hW' => ?_)
    refine Set.PairwiseDisjoint.countable_of_isOpen
      (s := fun T => proj Y y₀ '' (basic c W ∩ T)) ?_ ?_ ?_
    · rintro _ ⟨⟨c₁, rfl⟩, -⟩ _ ⟨⟨c₂, rfl⟩, -⟩ hne
      rw [Function.onFun, disjoint_left]
      rintro _ ⟨a, ⟨haS, ha1⟩, rfl⟩ ⟨b, ⟨hbS, hb2⟩, hab⟩
      have : b = a := injOn_basic (h𝒢₀s hW).2.2 c hbS haS hab
      subst this
      exact hne ((basic_eq_of_mem ha1).symm.trans (basic_eq_of_mem hb2))
    · rintro _ ⟨⟨c₁, rfl⟩, -⟩
      exact isOpenMap_proj _ ((isOpen_basic c (h𝒢₀s hW).1).inter (isOpen_basic c₁ (h𝒢₀s hW').1))
    · rintro T ⟨-, hne⟩
      exact hne.image _
  obtain ⟨𝒮', h𝒮'𝒮, h𝒮'c, h𝒮'u⟩ := exists_countable_cover_of_chain 𝒮 hopen hcov hnb
  have hF : {c : UniversalCover Y y₀ | c.pt = y₀}.Countable := by
    have : {c : UniversalCover Y y₀ | c.pt = y₀} ⊆ ⋃ S ∈ 𝒮', S ∩ {c | c.pt = y₀} := by
      intro c hc
      have : c ∈ ⋃₀ 𝒮' := h𝒮'u ▸ mem_univ c
      obtain ⟨S, hS, hcS⟩ := this
      exact mem_biUnion hS ⟨hcS, hc⟩
    refine Countable.mono this (h𝒮'c.biUnion fun S hS => Set.Subsingleton.countable ?_)
    obtain ⟨W, hW, c, -, rfl⟩ := h𝒮'𝒮 hS
    rintro a ⟨ha, ha'⟩ b ⟨hb, hb'⟩
    exact injOn_basic (h𝒢₀s hW).2.2 c ha hb (ha'.trans hb'.symm)
  haveI := hF.to_subtype
  refine Function.Injective.countable
    (f := fun g : FundamentalGroup Y y₀ =>
      (⟨⟨y₀, FundamentalGroup.toPath g⟩, rfl⟩ : {c : UniversalCover Y y₀ | c.pt = y₀})) ?_
  intro g h hgh
  have := congrArg Subtype.val hgh
  exact eq_of_heq (UniversalCover.mk.inj this).2

end UniversalCover

/-! ## Composite of covering maps -/

section Comp

open Function

variable {E X Z : Type*} [TopologicalSpace E] [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Z]

/-- **The composite of two covering maps is a covering map when the second one has finite
fibres.** The finite intersection of the images of the sheets is what makes the evenly covered
neighbourhood open. The composite of two coverings is *not* a covering in general (the classical
counterexamples live over a base that is not semilocally simply connected, of Hawaiian-earring
type); that failure is recorded, **not proved, here**. The other true variant is
`isCoveringMap_comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected`. -/
theorem isCoveringMap_comp_of_finite {q : E → X} {p : X → Z} (hp : IsCoveringMap p)
    (hq : IsCoveringMap q) (hfin : ∀ z, (p ⁻¹' {z}).Finite) : IsCoveringMap (p ∘ q) := by
  intro z
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hzU, S, hSo, hSi, -, hSs, hSd, hSc⟩ := IsEvenlyCovered.exists_sheets (hp z)
  haveI : Finite (p ⁻¹' {z}) := (hfin z).to_subtype
  have hy : ∀ i, ∃ y ∈ S i, p y = z := fun i => hSs i hzU
  choose y hyS hyp using hy
  choose V hVo hyV T hTo hTi _hTm hTs hTd hTc using
    fun i => IsEvenlyCovered.exists_sheets (hq (y i))
  set U' := U ∩ ⋂ i, p '' (S i ∩ V i) with hU'
  have hU'o : IsOpen U' :=
    hU.inter (isOpen_iInter_of_finite fun i => hp.isOpenMap _ ((hSo i).inter (hVo i)))
  have hzU' : z ∈ U' := ⟨hzU, mem_iInter.2 fun i => ⟨y i, ⟨hyS i, hyV i⟩, hyp i⟩⟩
  refine isEvenlyCovered_of_sheets (hp.continuous.comp hq.continuous)
    (hp.isOpenMap.comp hq.isOpenMap) hU'o hzU' (ι := Σ i, q ⁻¹' {y i})
    (fun k => T k.1 k.2 ∩ q ⁻¹' (S k.1 ∩ p ⁻¹' U')) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rintro ⟨i, j⟩
    exact (hTo i j).inter (((hSo i).inter (hU'o.preimage hp.continuous)).preimage hq.continuous)
  · rintro ⟨i, j⟩ e ⟨heT, heS, -⟩ e' ⟨he'T, he'S, -⟩ h
    exact hTi i j heT he'T (hSi i heS he'S h)
  · rintro ⟨i, j⟩ u hu
    obtain ⟨y', ⟨hy'S, hy'V⟩, rfl⟩ := mem_iInter.1 hu.2 i
    obtain ⟨e, he, rfl⟩ := hTs i j hy'V
    exact ⟨e, ⟨he, hy'S, hu⟩, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨i, j⟩ ⟨i', j'⟩ hne
    rw [Function.onFun, disjoint_left]
    rintro e ⟨heT, heS, -⟩ ⟨heT', heS', -⟩
    by_cases hii : i = i'
    · subst hii
      have hjj : j ≠ j' := fun h => hne (by rw [h])
      exact disjoint_left.1 (hTd i hjj) heT heT'
    · exact disjoint_left.1 (hSd hii) heS heS'
  · intro e he
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hSc he.1)
    obtain ⟨y', ⟨hy'S, hy'V⟩, hy'⟩ := mem_iInter.1 he.2 i
    have : y' = q e := hSi i hy'S hi hy'
    subst this
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hTc i hy'V)
    exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨i, j⟩, hj, hi, he⟩

/-- Paths lift through a composite of two covering maps. -/
theorem exists_path_lifts_comp {q : E → X} {p : X → Z} (hp : IsCoveringMap p)
    (hq : IsCoveringMap q) (δ : C(I, Z)) (e : E) (hδ : δ 0 = p (q e)) :
    ∃ Γ : C(I, E), (p ∘ q) ∘ Γ = δ ∧ Γ 0 = e := by
  let Γ₁ := hp.liftPath δ (q e) hδ
  let Γ₂ := hq.liftPath Γ₁ e (hp.liftPath_zero δ (q e) hδ)
  refine ⟨Γ₂, ?_, hq.liftPath_zero _ _ _⟩
  rw [Function.comp_assoc, hq.liftPath_lifts, hp.liftPath_lifts]

/-- If a path of `E` is sent by `p ∘ q` to a loop null-homotopic rel endpoints in `Z`, it is a
loop. -/
theorem eq_of_comp_homotopicRel_const {q : E → X} {p : X → Z} (hp : IsCoveringMap p)
    (hq : IsCoveringMap q) {a b : E} (γ : Path a b)
    (h : (ContinuousMap.comp ⟨p ∘ q, hp.continuous.comp hq.continuous⟩
      γ.toContinuousMap).HomotopicRel (ContinuousMap.const I (p (q a))) {0, 1}) : b = a := by
  have h1 : (ContinuousMap.comp ⟨q, hq.continuous⟩ γ.toContinuousMap).HomotopicRel
      (ContinuousMap.const I (q a)) {0, 1} :=
    (hp.homotopicRel_iff_comp (f₀ := ContinuousMap.comp ⟨q, hq.continuous⟩ γ.toContinuousMap)
      (f₁ := ContinuousMap.const I (q a)) (S := ({0, 1} : Set I))
      ⟨0, Or.inl rfl, by simp⟩).mpr h
  have h2 : γ.toContinuousMap.HomotopicRel (ContinuousMap.const I a) {0, 1} :=
    (hq.homotopicRel_iff_comp (f₀ := γ.toContinuousMap) (f₁ := ContinuousMap.const I a)
      (S := ({0, 1} : Set I)) ⟨0, Or.inl rfl, by simp⟩).mpr h1
  simpa using h2.fst_eq_snd (Or.inr rfl : (1 : I) ∈ ({0, 1} : Set I))

/-- **The composite of two covering maps is a covering map over a locally path-connected,
semilocally simply connected base** (no hypothesis on the fibres, on `X` or on `E`). The sheets
over a good path-connected neighbourhood `W` of `z` are the path components of `(p ∘ q) ⁻¹' W`;
a path in one of them between two points of a fibre is sent to a loop null-homotopic in `Z`,
which lifts through `p` and then `q` (`eq_of_comp_homotopicRel_const`). -/
theorem isCoveringMap_comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected {q : E → X} {p : X → Z}
    (hp : IsCoveringMap p) (hq : IsCoveringMap q) [LocPathConnectedSpace Z]
    (hZ : SemilocallySimplyConnected Z) : IsCoveringMap (p ∘ q) := by
  intro z
  set f := p ∘ q with hfdef
  have hfc : Continuous f := hp.continuous.comp hq.continuous
  have hfl : IsLocalHomeomorph f := hp.isLocalHomeomorph.comp hq.isLocalHomeomorph
  haveI : LocPathConnectedSpace E := locPathConnectedSpace_of_isLocalHomeomorph hfl
  obtain ⟨W, hWo, hzW, -, hWc, hWg⟩ := exists_isGoodSet hZ z univ_mem
  -- the key: a path in `f ⁻¹' W` between two points of one fibre is a loop
  have key : ∀ a b : E, JoinedIn (f ⁻¹' W) a b → f a = f b → a = b := by
    intro a b hab hf
    let γ := hab.somePath
    have hγ : ∀ t, f (γ t) ∈ W := hab.somePath_mem
    let β : Path (f a) (f a) := (γ.map hfc).cast rfl hf
    have ha : f a ∈ W := by simpa using hγ 0
    have hH := hWg β (Path.refl (f a)) (fun t => hγ t) (fun _ => ha)
    have := eq_of_comp_homotopicRel_const hp hq γ ?_
    · exact this.symm
    · obtain ⟨H⟩ := hH
      exact ⟨H⟩
  -- lifting a path of `W` gives a path of `f ⁻¹' W`
  have lift : ∀ (e : E) (w : Z), f e ∈ W → w ∈ W →
      ∃ e', f e' = w ∧ JoinedIn (f ⁻¹' W) e e' := by
    intro e w he hw
    obtain ⟨δ, hδ⟩ := hWc.joinedIn (f e) he w hw
    obtain ⟨Γ, hΓ, hΓ0⟩ := exists_path_lifts_comp hp hq δ.toContinuousMap e (by simp [hfdef])
    have hΓt : ∀ t, f (Γ t) = δ t := fun t => congrFun hΓ t
    refine ⟨Γ 1, by rw [hΓt]; simp, ⟨{ toContinuousMap := Γ, source' := hΓ0, target' := rfl },
      fun t => ?_⟩⟩
    change f (Γ t) ∈ W
    rw [hΓt]; exact hδ t
  refine isEvenlyCovered_of_sheets hfc hfl.isOpenMap hWo hzW (ι := f ⁻¹' {z})
    (fun e => pathComponentIn (f ⁻¹' W) e.1)
    (fun e => (hWo.preimage hfc).pathComponentIn _) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rintro e a ha b hb hab
    exact key a b ((show JoinedIn _ e.1 a from ha).symm.trans hb) hab
  · rintro e w hw
    have hfe : f e.1 ∈ W := by rw [show f e.1 = z from e.2]; exact hzW
    obtain ⟨e', he', hj⟩ := lift e.1 w hfe hw
    exact ⟨e', hj, he'⟩
  · rintro e e' hne
    rw [Function.onFun, disjoint_left]
    intro c hc hc'
    apply hne
    refine Subtype.ext (key _ _ ((show JoinedIn _ e.1 c from hc).trans
      (show JoinedIn _ e'.1 c from hc').symm) ?_)
    rw [show f e.1 = z from e.2, show f e'.1 = z from e'.2]
  · intro a ha
    obtain ⟨b, hb, hj⟩ := lift a z ha hzW
    exact mem_iUnion.2 ⟨⟨b, hb⟩, hj.symm⟩

/-- Alias of `isCoveringMap_comp_of_finite` under the dispatch's name; after `open GX` it is
reachable by dot notation, `hp.comp_of_finite hq hfin`. -/
alias IsCoveringMap.comp_of_finite := isCoveringMap_comp_of_finite

/-- Alias of `isCoveringMap_comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected` (dot notation after `open GX`). -/
alias IsCoveringMap.comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected :=
  isCoveringMap_comp_of_semilocallySimplyConnected

end Comp

end GX
